<title>USA: Mellon Bank issues $100 million bank notes.</title>
<headline>Mellon Bank issues $100 million bank notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue was priced on Thursday via sole lead manager Chase Securities Inc. The notes are all sold on Thursday morning, according to the Chase syndicate desk.</p>
<p>BORROWER MELLON BANK CORP</p>
<p>AMT $100 MLN	    COUPON  6.44 PCT  MATURITY 03/06/98</p>
<p>TYPE BANK NOTES	 ISS PRICE 100.00  PAY DATE 09/06/96</p>
<p>LAST MOODY A1	   REOFFER N.A.	PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-PLUS	 YIELD  6.44 PCT   CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>INDUSTRY BANKING</p>
</text>
